  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "In the restaurant, Nastya stops Kostya because she wants to have a very serious conversation, and we will listen to their dialogue in Russian first; do not worry about catching every single word.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Костя, нам надо поговорить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Это может подождать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нет, это важно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Настя, я так по тебе соскучился.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Пожалуйста, послушай меня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Я тебя слушаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Наши отношения развиваются быстро.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Я думаю, это отлично.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Но нам надо обсудить наше будущее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "У нас есть много времени.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нет, время пришло сейчас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Хорошо, я готов поговорить.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let us break down this interaction.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Костя, нам надо поговорить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Kostya, we have to talk.' Russian expresses this impersonally, literally saying 'to me' or 'to you' with 'to talk'. Then Kostya replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Это может подождать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Can it wait?' Notice the word order: 'this' comes first, and 'to wait' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нет, это важно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No, it is important.' Here 'this' sets up the idea, while 'important' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Настя, я так по тебе соскучился.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Nastya, I have missed you so much.' Notice the word order: 'Nastya' comes first, and 'missed' finishes the sentence. And Nastya jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Пожалуйста, послушай меня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Please, listen to me.' In Russian, 'listen' leads into 'me' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Я тебя слушаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am listening to you.' Kostya starts with 'I' and pairs it with 'you' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Наши отношения развиваются быстро.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Our relationship is moving fast.' Nastya puts 'relations' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'develop'. Kostya answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Я думаю, это отлично.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I think this is great.' The key word here means 'I', which Kostya combines with 'I think'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Но нам надо обсудить наше будущее.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'But we need to discuss our future.' The first content word means 'us', and 'future' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "У нас есть много времени.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We have a lot of time.' A compact expression built around 'us' and 'time'. Then Nastya replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нет, время пришло сейчас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No, the time is now.' Notice the word order: 'time' comes first, and 'now' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Хорошо, я готов поговорить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Okay, I am ready to talk.' Listen for the word meaning 'good' right alongside 'I' in this line. Now let us listen to the conversation again without interruption.",
      "gap": 0.9
